# Derived from the existing sources (Task 15); the tree has NOT been
# reformatted with it yet (Task 25 does that in one formatting-only commit).
# `make format-diffstat` reports how many lines it would change.
#
# What the code already does, measured over src/ and tests/ (208K lines):
#   - 2-space indent (no tabs), braces attached (15.4K attached vs 0.3K on
#     their own line), namespaces not indented, access specifiers at +1;
#   - `T* x` / `T& x` (16.9K + 5.0K) against `T *x` / `T &x` (0.2K);
#   - 99.65% of lines are under 120 columns; the older modules wrap near 80
#     and the newer ones near 120, so 120 is the limit both satisfy;
#   - short `if (...) return x;` and short loops stay on one line (7.1K
#     one-line ifs against 0.8K broken ones), `else` chains included;
#   - includes are grouped (own header, then <system>, then "project") but
#     not sorted inside a group, and some orders matter (the Mbed TLS user
#     config, the Unikraft shims), so includes are left alone.
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: Google
Standard: c++17
ColumnLimit: 120
IndentWidth: 2
UseTab: Never
AccessModifierOffset: -1
NamespaceIndentation: None
BreakBeforeBraces: Attach
DerivePointerAlignment: false
PointerAlignment: Left
ReferenceAlignment: Pointer
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: AllIfsAndElse
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: true
AllowShortBlocksOnASingleLine: Always
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: All
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: true
IndentCaseLabels: true
SortIncludes: Never
IncludeBlocks: Preserve
SortUsingDeclarations: Never
